 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Keel overlay: Nginx, the front of Keel Web
 The Nginx overlay of Keel Linux (handbook decisions 0030, 0036 and 0042):
 trixie's nginx, used as it is, and the overlay manifest keel reads,
 installed as /usr/share/keel/overlays/nginx.yaml (decision 0041).
 .
 It adds to Debian's layout, without editing nginx.conf: /keel-health,
 answering 204 on the loopback addresses only, for the manifest's check;
 a stream block reading /etc/nginx/streams-enabled/; and /run/nginx for
 the sockets of Keel Web's internal hops. Debian's default site is left
 as it is. nginx.service stays enabled, the state of every installation
 mode.
